<prefabs>
	<!-- Crew platform for the Mumakil war tower (#627 phase 2). Invisible in game: every mesh here is
	     visible_only_when_editing, and the tower the player sees is sk_mumakil_platform_a1, an AdditionalMesh on
	     the Horse item taom_mumakil. This prefab only gives the crew somewhere to stand and the engine somewhere
	     to put them.

	     SCALE. Authored MOUNT-LOCAL, 1:1 with sk_mumakil_harad_01.fbx, which is drawn at elephant scale. The
	     engine grows the mount to 3.0x from the Horse item's BodyLength=300, and TaomMumakilPlatform scales this
	     whole entity by the mount's Agent.AgentScale every tick, so the 3.0 is never written down here. Change
	     BodyLength and the crew follow; bake the 3.0 in and they would end up inside the beast.

	     DECKS, measured in Blender 2026-09-20 from the platform mesh's upward faces and its wall faces:
	       main  z 3.00 authored =  9.00 m in game, 15.0 m2 standable inside the walls, ceiling 47 archers
	       upper z 3.80 authored = 11.40 m in game,  2.6 m2 standable, ceiling 14
	       nest  z 4.60 authored = 13.80 m in game,  1.9 m2 standable, ceiling 5
	     Those are geometric ceilings at the 0.74 m rule, not a crew. Mike settled the crew at eight: five, two and
	     one (2026-09-20). Every frame below was CHOSEN from the points Blender proved are both on the deck and a
	     body's radius clear of a wall, then spread as far apart as that set allows.

	     SPACING is the rule that decides how many archers any platform can carry, here and on the howdah: two
	     0.37 m body capsules closer than 0.74 m overlap, the engine shoves them apart every frame, the seat
	     teleports them back, and the engine then reads tens of m/s of movement, at which point no bow draw ever
	     completes. That cost the howdah nine in-game rounds (#627). MumakilPlatformTests checks the spacing AFTER
	     scaling, in world metres.

	     HEADROOM is the second rule, and it is the one a multi-deck platform adds that the howdah never had. A
	     crew frame under a higher deck's floor needs the human capsule's full 1.92 m of world clearance (radius
	     0.37, pos1 z 1.55, Native/monsters.xml): barrier is in the engine's missile-exclusion mask but NOT in its
	     agent mask, so an archer whose head is inside the deck above is shoved every frame and put back by its
	     seat, which is the same velocity failure as bad spacing and just as invisible. Every deck underside sits
	     0.598 authored below the deck above, which is 1.79 m in game, so a frame under one CANNOT pass: the only
	     fix is to move it out from under, and the footprint it must clear is inflated by the capsule's radius,
	     not just its centre. mumakil_crew_main_4 was authored at y -0.936, directly beneath the upper deck, and
	     moved to (0.700, -0.500) beside it on 2026-09-20.

	     The two rules pull against each other, which is why both are pinned: the first move out from under the
	     upper deck put main_4 1.05 m from main_1, and at a 0.45 m deadband two archers drifting at each other
	     would close to 0.15 m, inside the spacing rule. The kept position is clear of the deck above AND 2.52 m
	     from its nearest neighbour. MumakilPlatformTests pins headroom, containment, spacing and that margin.

	     The Armory is unversioned, so the repo keeps a byte-identical snapshot at
	     docs/reference/lotrlome-armory-snapshot/Prefabs/taom_mumakil_platform.xml. -->
